A `---` inside a value or an indented block-scalar line is content, not the closing delimiter:
the keys after it still reach the row, so a `where` on them matches.

-- fixtures/cwd/.booping --
project_name: probe
vault_path: ./vault
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/alpha/index.md --
---
title: before --- after
notes: |
  first
  ---
  last
status: done
---

body
-- fixtures/cwd/vault/plans/beta/index.md --
---
title: Beta
status: ready-for-dev
---

body
-- cmd --
booping query --glob 'plans/*/index.md' --where status=done --columns slug,title
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
| slug | title | path |
| --- | --- | --- |
| alpha | before --- after | plans/alpha/index.md |
-- stderr --
